DESCRIPTION:Wednesday 11/11 · 12:00 PM to 1:00 PM\n\nJoey Brackner\, Alaba
 ma's state folklorist from 1985 until he retired in 2022\, talks about the
  19th century pottery makers of Alabama. The talk places the potters in th
 e politics of their time\, including enslavement\, secession\, Reconstruct
 ion and the populist movement. The History Museum of Mobile hosts the free
  Learning Lunch series\, and guests are invited to bring their lunch.\n\nP
 rice: Free\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-hmm-learning
